GOAL: fix the bug in the `isInDST` getter in /luxon/src/datetime.js (around lines 1160-1172).

CURRENT (buggy) CODE:

  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1 }).offset || this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
      );
    }
  }

The bug: `this.set({ month: 1 })` keeps the current day-of-month, so it does not reliably give a standard-time (non-DST) reference point. In 1974 the USA was on DST for the whole year from January 6 to October 27, so for e.g. 1974-06-15 the January reference is also DST and `isInDST` wrongly returns false.

FIX: use `this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 })` as the January reference. The resulting getter must be exactly:

  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset ||
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
      )
    }
  }

Keep the JSDoc comment above it unchanged. Do not change anything else in the repo.

