GOAL: fix `padStart` in /luxon/src/impl/util.js (lines ~101-107). It pads by slicing the concatenated string, which corrupts negative numbers: `padStart(-10, 4)` returns "00-10" instead of "-0010". This makes `DateTime.fromObject({ year: -10, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toISODate()` return "00-10-05-25" instead of the ISO 8601 expanded form "-0010-05-25".

CURRENT (buggy) CODE:

  export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
    if (input.toString().length < n) {
      return ("0".repeat(n) + input).slice(-n);
    } else {
      return input.toString();
    }
  }

FIX: pad the digits and keep the minus sign in front, without changing the existing behaviour for non-negative inputs (in particular, inputs whose digit string is already at least n characters long must NOT be truncated, e.g. padStart(118040, 4) must stay "118040" and padStart(1982, 2) must stay "1982"). Replace the function with exactly:

  export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
    const isNeg = input < 0,
      digits = (isNeg ? -input : input).toString();
    if (digits.length < n) {
      return (isNeg ? "-" : "") + ("0".repeat(n) + digits).slice(-n);
    } else {
      return (isNeg ? "-" : "") + digits;
    }
  }

